{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_36", "type": "agent_message", "text": "{\"slug\":\"us-durable-goods-shipments-mom-june-2026\",\"country\":\"US\",\"type\":\"data\",\"title\":\"US Durable Goods Shipments MoM, Jun 2026\",\"question\":\"First-print month-over-month percent growth in U.S. Census Bureau M3 Manufacturers' Value of Shipments: Durable Goods (AMDMVS), seasonally adjusted, for June 2026.\",\"unit\":\"percent_growth\",\"pointEstimate\":0.6,\"ciLow\":-0.22,\"ciHigh\":1.42,\"confidence\":0.8,\"resolutionDate\":\"2026-07-27\",\"resolutionSource\":\"U.S. Census Bureau M3 Advance Report, mirrored in ALFRED/FRED series AMDMVS\",\"resolutionSourceUrl\":\"https://alfred.stlouisfed.org/graph/alfredgraph.csv?id=AMDMVS\",\"resolutionRule\":\"Use the first official June 2026 print released with the Census M3 Advance Report on Durable Goods at 8:30 a.m. on 2026-07-27. Resolve as 100*(June 2026 seasonally adjusted AMDMVS level minus May 2026 seasonally adjusted AMDMVS level)/(May 2026 seasonally adjusted AMDMVS level), in percent, using the first-print vintage; later revisions do not change resolution. The ledger sourceBinding points to AMDMVS with a multiply transform even though the target unit is percent_growth, so the forecast is tied to the same target and interprets the target as the month-over-month percent growth implied by AMDMVS levels.\",\"dataPointId\":\"census.m3.durable_goods_shipments_mom.2026_06.first_print\",\"historicalContext\":[{\"label\":\"2026-05 m/m from AMDMVS levels\",\"value\":1.0044093014090059},{\"label\":\"2026-04 m/m from AMDMVS levels\",\"value\":0.6838995293927989},{\"label\":\"2026-03 m/m from AMDMVS levels\",\"value\":0.7933804757783034},{\"label\":\"2026-02 m/m from AMDMVS levels\",\"value\":1.5626834740827487},{\"label\":\"2026-05 AMDMVS level, millions USD SA\",\"value\":328030}],\"drivers\":[\"Recent AMDMVS shipments momentum was positive through May 2026\",\"Durable-goods shipments are volatile but less aircraft-order-driven than new orders\",\"Mean reversion from unusually firm early-2026 monthly gains\",\"First-print target uses seasonally adjusted AMDMVS levels and excludes later revisions\"],\"sourceContext\":[\"https://www.census.gov/manufacturing/m3/release_schedule.html\",\"https://fred.stlouisfed.org/data/AMDMVS\",\"https://fred.stlouisfed.org/series/AMDMVS\",\"https://alfred.stlouisfed.org/series?seid=AMDMVS\"],\"runAt\":\"2026-07-26T00:59:51Z\",\"reasoning\":[{\"kind\":\"heading\",\"text\":\"Forecast for June 2026 Durable Goods Shipments MoM\"},{\"kind\":\"text\",\"text\":\"Framing and exact resolver: the target is Census M3 durable-goods shipments, seasonally adjusted AMDMVS, June 2026 first print. The Census release schedule verifies the June 2026 Advance Report date as 2026-07-27, with the Full Report on 2026-08-04; I use the advance first print only.\"},{\"kind\":\"tool\",\"tool\":\"official.lookup\",\"call\":\"Opened Census M3 release schedule for June 2026 advance and full report dates.\",\"result\":\"Fetched schedule row: June 2026 Advance Report on Durable Goods and Advance Total Manufacturing = 7/27/2026 at 8:30 a.m.; Full Report = 8/4/2026 at 10:00 a.m.\"},{\"kind\":\"tool\",\"tool\":\"official.lookup\",\"call\":\"Opened FRED/ALFRED AMDMVS series page to verify series identity, source, units, latest observation, and next release.\",\"result\":\"Fetched AMDMVS identity: Manufacturers' Value of Shipments: Durable Goods; source U.S. Census Bureau; units Millions of Dollars, Seasonally Adjusted; latest May 2026 = 328,030; next release date = Jul 27, 2026.\"},{\"kind\":\"tool\",\"tool\":\"official.lookup\",\"call\":\"Opened FRED table data for AMDMVS and read recent levels used to compute same-variant month-over-month growth.\",\"result\":\"Fetched AMDMVS levels, millions of dollars SA: Dec 2025 = 312,260; Jan 2026 = 315,099; Feb 2026 = 320,023; Mar 2026 = 322,562; Apr 2026 = 324,768; May 2026 = 328,030.\"},{\"kind\":\"tool\",\"tool\":\"calculator\",\"call\":\"Computed recent month-over-month percent changes from fetched AMDMVS levels.\",\"result\":\"Fetched-level calculations: Feb 2026 m/m = 100*(320,023-315,099)/315,099 = 1.5627; Mar 2026 = 0.7934; Apr 2026 = 0.6839; May 2026 = 1.0044 percent.\"},{\"kind\":\"text\",\"text\":\"Variant discipline: every anchor is AMDMVS, Manufacturers' Value of Shipments: Durable Goods, seasonally adjusted, monthly. I did not mix not-seasonally-adjusted shipments, new orders, excluding-transportation series, or full-report revisions into the first-print target.\"},{\"kind\":\"text\",\"text\":\"Base rate/reference class: the 2024-02 through 2026-05 AMDMVS month-over-month changes have a mean of 0.455 percentage points, while the latest four reported changes were all positive at 1.563, 0.793, 0.684, and 1.004 percent, so the base rate is modest positive growth with unusually firm recent momentum.\"},{\"kind\":\"math\",\"text\":\"Prior/update/interval: persistence prior is the 2024-02 to 2026-05 AMDMVS m/m reference class. Historical sample = 28 monthly percent changes computed from fetched AMDMVS levels; mean = 0.455. Adjustment components: +0.20 for broad early-2026 positive momentum, -0.05 for mean reversion after four consecutive gains, giving point = 0.60. Interval method uses realized dispersion of the m/m percent changes: sum of squares = 16.9229, sigma = sqrt((16.9229 - 28*0.4550^2)/27) = 0.642 percentage points, so 1.28*sigma = 0.822; point 0.60 +/- 0.82 gives [-0.22, 1.42].\"},{\"kind\":\"text\",\"text\":\"Counter-consideration: upside risk is a stronger transportation-equipment or machinery shipment month that would land above the interval, especially if June catches delayed May shipments. Downside risk is a pullback after the strong January-May level rise or a volatile transportation drop; a broad reversal below about -0.22 percent would land outside the interval on the low side.\"},{\"kind\":\"forecast\",\"point\":0.6,\"ciLow\":-0.22,\"ciHigh\":1.42}]}"}}
